    "created_at": "2017-04-13T20:52:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-13T20:52:34Z",
    "body": "I can't say we considered anything else. I think it'd be pretty confusing to depart from the typical extended-attributes-go-in-square-brackets-before-the-thing-they-modify pattern. But it would indeed help avoid the need to \"flow through\" certain extended attributes from e.g. non-required dictionary members to their types. I'd be open to changing it if we really think it's compelling.\r\n\r\nI agree remembering to do the right thing is a bit hard, but I'm hopeful that with proper validation tooling spec authors and implementers will get it right.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
